BT /F1 10 Tf 50 720 Td (IN THE MADRAS HIGH COURT \(MADURAI BENCH\)
CASE NO: C.M.A.\(MD\) No. 1450 of 2026
CNR NUMBER: HCMD011023452026
YEAR: 2026

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Justice R. Vijayakumar

PARTIES:
The Divisional Manager, New India Assurance Co. Ltd.
... Petitioner\(s\) / Appellant\(s\)
Versus
Veluchamy \(Injured Quarry Worker\)
... Respondent\(s\)

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Employee's Compensation Act 1923

SECTIONS & PROVISIONS:
Employee's Compensation Act Section 3, Employee's Compensation Act Section 4

KEY TOPICS & ISSUES:
Workmen Compensation, Functional Disability, Total Incapacity, Employment Injury, Occupational Hazard

================================================================================
                                   JUDGMENT
================================================================================

1. FACTS OF THE CASE:
Quarry blaster suffered right arm amputation. Insurance company argued medical board assessed physical disability at only 65%.

2. ISSUES FRAMED:
Should compensation be assessed on medical physical disability or functional loss of earning capacity?

3. LEGAL RATIO & FINDINGS:
Functional disability must be assessed based on the specific vocational work performed by the workman; 65% physical disability equals 100% functional loss.

4. FINAL ORDER:
Civil Miscellaneous Appeal Dismissed; 100% loss of earning capacity upheld for quarry blaster suffering limb amputation.

Ordered and decreed accordingly.

Hon'ble Justice R. Vijayakumar
Madras High Court \(Madurai Bench\)
[LEXGUARD REPOSITORY CRYPTOGRAPHIC SEAL]
) Tj ET
